          %h2#idea Idea
          %blockquote
            %p
              %em Der unendlich kleinste Theil des Raumes ist immer ein Raum, etwas, das Continuität hat, nicht aber ein blosser Punct
              (
              %a{:href => "Grundriss+des+Eigenth&#252;mlichen+der+Wissenschaftslehre#4IVUnendlichKleinsterTeilDesRaumes"}> Fichte 1795, Grundriss §4.IV
              )
            %p (“An infinitesimally small part of space is always a space, something with continuity, but not a bare point.”)
          %p
            An infinitesimal neighbourhood is a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal"} infinitesimal
            diameter”. This can be made precise in several formalisms, including
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonstandard+analysis"} nonstandard analysis
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+spaces"} ringed spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
          %p#MonadTerminology
            %strong “Monads”.
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonstandard+analysis"} nonstandard analysis
            the infinitesimal neighbourhood of a point is traditionally called (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#InNonstandardAnalysis"} below
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+%28disambiguation%29"} monad
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "monad+disambiguation#HistoricalOrigins"} ancient terminology going back to Euclid
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "monad+disambiguation#HistoricalOrigins"} there
          %p
            Curiously, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            the construction of all infinitesimal neighbourhoods (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk+bundle"} infinitesimal disk bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            in the sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            (see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "infinitesimal+disk+bundle#MonadicityAdjointToJetBundles"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+monad"} adjoint monad
            to the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+comonad"} jet comonad
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "monad#Etymology"} Etymology
